          {
            "type": "miscellaneous",
            "text": "The killer phenotype requires the presence of two different dsRNA viruses: an L-A helper virus and the toxin-coding (M) killer virus. Killer strains of S.cerevisiae producing the toxin K1 kill sensitive cells but are resistant to their own toxin. The gamma and delta chains may play a role, on there own or as part of the protoxin, in the self-protection of the virus-infected killer yeast (toxin immunity).",
